  "body": "In a few places the spec links to `POST /_matrix/client/r0/account/3pid`:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-doc/blob/315cf67f6b713e0bfeb99527767e2d65c4d8e11f/specification/client_server_api.rst#L710\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-doc/blob/315cf67f6b713e0bfeb99527767e2d65c4d8e11f/specification/client_server_api.rst#L989\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-doc/blob/315cf67f6b713e0bfeb99527767e2d65c4d8e11f/specification/client_server_api.rst#L1009\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-doc/blob/315cf67f6b713e0bfeb99527767e2d65c4d8e11f/specification/client_server_api.rst#L1047\r\n\r\nThese links don't work. I think this is because the API is now deprecated, so its ID is `deprecated-post-matrix-client-r0-account-3pid`, not `post-matrix-client-r0-account-3pid`.\r\n\r\nI would have just fixed this in https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-doc/pull/2988, but then thought: if it's deprecated, should we not update the spec content to stop suggesting that people use it?\r\n",
